X:1
T:Whiskey in the Jar
C:Traditional (Laws L13)
S:Melody after a transcription in G by Alf Warnock (folktunefinder.com, tune 104973); no printed source cited
N:Transposed from G to D for baritones. Written in treble clef; men sing an octave below written pitch (A2 to D4).
N:The source has no lyric underlay; the fit of the words is my own. Where a line has more syllables than notes,
N:an eighth is split into two sixteenths of the same pitch (bars 3, 5, 6, 9).
N:Chorus chords follow the usual session harmony; the source marks no chords in bars 10-11.
N:Sing the chorus after each verse. Verses 2-5 are printed below the music.
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=110
K:D
