w:Whack for my dad-dy-o, There's whis-key in the jar.
W:
W:2. I counted out his money and it made a pretty penny,
W:   I put it in my pocket and I took it home to Jenny.
W:   She sighed and she swore that she never would deceive me,
W:   But the devil take the women, for they never can be easy.
W:
W:3. I went up to my chamber all for to take a slumber,
W:   I dreamt of gold and jewels and for sure it was no wonder.
W:   But Jenny drew my charges and she filled them up with water,
W:   Then sent for Captain Farrell to be ready for the slaughter.
W:
W:4. 'Twas early in the morning, just before I rose to travel,
W:   Up comes a band of footmen and likewise Captain Farrell.
W:   I first produced my pistol, for she stole away my rapier,
W:   I couldn't shoot the water, so a prisoner I was taken.
W:
W:5. If anyone can aid me, 'tis my brother in the army,
W:   If I can find his station in Cork or in Killarney.
W:   And if he'll go with me, we'll go roving in Kilkenny,
W:   And I'm sure he'll treat me better than my own a-sporting Jenny.
